            <div xml:id="d129">

                <pb facs="0106" n="98" sameAs="frus:frus1939v05/pg98"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">862.8591/598: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Chile</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Bowers</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-12-16T12:00:00-04:00">December 16,
                            1939—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 12:05 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>228. Informed by Foreign Minister late last night that <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Dusseldorf</hi> was taken in custody by British and not sunk. He said it
                    will have to be taken to a British port. See telegram this morning from Vice
                    Consul at Antofagasta.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bowers</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
